            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "`ctx_saved_curwin()` is called twice in the ternary when computing `stl_curwin`. Besides being slightly wasteful, it can (in theory) yield inconsistent results if the saved window becomes invalid between calls. Store the result once and then fall back to `curwin`.",
            "commit_id": "5b13db03387494d042f63a7e7ad10f95359a5b10",
            "created_at": "2026-08-05T16:25:13Z",
            "diff_hunk": "@@ -91,14 +91,19 @@ void win_redr_status(win_T *wp)\n \n   busy = true;\n   wp->w_redr_status = false;\n-  if (wp->w_status_height == 0 && !(is_stl_global && wp == curwin)) {\n+\n+  // curwin may be temporarily switched during autocmds (ctx_switch).\n+  win_T *stl_curwin = ctx_saved_curwin() != NULL ? ctx_saved_curwin() : curwin;\n+  bool is_stl_curwin = wp == stl_curwin;",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/41169#discussion_r3722259279",
